invariant: INV-26
file: quic_packet.c
catches: test/lint-invariants.sh
reason: quic_hp_mask writes the header protection mask with the AES
  form of RFC 9001 §5.4.3 instead of the ChaCha20 form of §5.4.4, so
  aes_encrypt_block reads a header protection key quic_hp_key_init
  derived from a TLS traffic secret. That is the one thing INV-26
  forbids: a secret key reaching a table-driven cipher.
  inv-26-aes-public-keys-only matches the call, because quic_packet.c
  is not one of the two files the rule excludes.

--- old
    // CH_QUIC_STUB: not implemented yet; this call fails closed and writes nothing.
    (void)h;
    (void)sample;
    (void)mask;
}
--- new
    uint8_t block[AES_BLOCK];
    aes_encrypt_block((const aes_public_key *)h, sample, block);
    for (size_t i = 0; i < QUIC_HP_MASK_LEN; i++) {
        mask[i] = block[i];
    }
}
